{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":0,"id":10,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.10","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.local.lf83|0:on_enter","journal_text":"At Claywater Station on the Blackwood Road, I paid Livia Varinius, the well-keeper, for my stop on the station bank, and Signs-For-The-Cargo, the landing's poler, wants a drake from every walker who wades the ford. Travellers pay twice for one stop. I'm to hear each keeper's side. Livia keeps the well by the station house door; Signs-For-The-Cargo works the plank raft at the landing stage, across the ford to the north.","directions":"From the Blackwood Road: Claywater Station is about six hundred yards west of the signpost at Cartwright's Cross, where the arms point to Gideon and to Leyawiin. Going west, the station house roof shows first, on the right of the road. The well stands at the station house door, inside the low stone walls. From the well, the ford is about sixty yards to the north; the plank raft and the landing stage are at the water, with the round mud huts behind them on the far bank. If the road runs on into open marsh with no roofs in sight, you have passed it."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":1,"id":20,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.20","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.local.lf83|1:on_enter","journal_text":"At Claywater Station, Livia Varinius charges every traveller two drakes for the stop, to pay a mason to re-line the well in stone, and Signs-For-The-Cargo charges walkers a drake a head at the ford, because the landing worked the ford before the well was dug and will not haul stone for it. The rains are about seven days off. I'm to find out why the well is failing, and to win back the clay bend below the raft, where a crocodile now lies and the landing's clay basket was dropped. Takes-The-Short-Weight, at the round mud hut on the landing bank, judges everything by its water.","directions":"The crack is in the well head itself, on the side that faces the ford; Livia's jar sits on the coping beside it, and her ledger lies on the counter inside the station house. The clay bend is downstream of the raft: from the end of the landing stage, follow the landing bank east about fifty yards to where the bank turns and the water runs deep and dark under a bare clay cut. If the bank turns to reeds and open marsh, you have passed it. Takes-The-Short-Weight lives in the round mud hut on the landing bank, about forty yards north of the raft, past the drying racks."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":2,"id":30,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.30","journal_text":"The well at Claywater Station is failing because its stone head has cracked on the ford side and the ford comes in through the crack. Stone cracks in that clay bank, and clay pressed in behind it would hold. I have killed the crocodile at the clay bend below the raft and have the landing's clay basket. The station charged first, the landing charged in answer, and between them travellers wade at the bend at night. I'm to put terms to Livia Varinius at the well and to Signs-For-The-Cargo at the raft before the rains, about seven days from when I came. Livia's objections: mud has no place in an Imperial well, and the landing would take half a charge for water it never draws. Signs-For-The-Cargo's: the landing will not haul stone, and it will not pay for water it does not drink.","directions":"Livia Varinius is at the well by day and at the station house counter in the evening; Signs-For-The-Cargo is at the raft by day."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":3,"id":40,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.40","ending":"complete","journal_text":"I brought Livia Varinius and Signs-For-The-Cargo to terms at Claywater Station: one charge for the stop, split between the station and the landing, and the landing will press clay behind the cracked well head before the rains. I killed the crocodile at the clay bend and gave the landing back its basket. No mason will be sent for, and the waders have no reason to cross at the bend now.","ending_id":"e-shared"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":4,"id":41,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.41","ending":"complete","journal_text":"Travellers at Claywater Station paid at the well and again at the ford. I paid Signs-For-The-Cargo a hundred drakes to take no charge from walkers this season, so they pay once, at the well. Livia Varinius still saves for her mason, the well is still cracked, and the landing has no clay for its walls.","ending_id":"e-station"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":5,"id":42,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.42","ending":"complete","journal_text":"Travellers at Claywater Station paid at the well and again at the ford. I learned the well's stone head has cracked, and rather than have that said aloud, Livia Varinius has dropped her charge on the stop. Travellers pay once, at the landing. The well is still cracked, and no mason will come.","ending_id":"e-landing"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":6,"id":90,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.90","ending":"failed","journal_text":"I made no terms at Claywater Station before the rains came. The landing has no clay for its walls, the well is still cracked, and travellers still pay at both banks or wade at the bend.","ending_id":"e-rains"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":7,"id":92,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.92","ending":"failed","journal_text":"I learned that Livia Varinius is dead. Nobody keeps the well at Claywater Station now; it is boarded over, the station's charge has died with her, and the landing keeps its charge on the ford. The two charges will never be settled.","ending_id":"e-keeper-dead"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lf83","ord":8,"id":93,"place":"place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station","journal":"text.journal.lf83.93","ending":"failed","journal_text":"I learned that Signs-For-The-Cargo is dead. Nobody at Claywater Station poles the raft, and the landing will make no terms with the station while it mourns. Both charges stand.","ending_id":"e-poler-dead"}
