{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh37","ord":1,"id":20,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh37.20","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.local.lh37|1:on_enter"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh37","ord":2,"id":30,"place":"place.hist-heartland.nine-trunks","journal":"text.journal.lh37.30","outside_packet":"4.2.hist-heartland"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh37","ord":3,"id":90,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh37.90","ending":"failed"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":0,"id":10,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.10","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.local.lh38|0:on_enter","journal_text":"Mee-Sei, who cooks at the fire stand in Greenspring, told me that guests at the lodge have been falling sick, and that people blame his food. I'm to find out what is making them ill.","directions":"The pool lies under the Hist, a few steps from the fire stand; the lodge, where the sick guests lie, faces it across the spring."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":1,"id":20,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.20","journal_text":"The guests at the Greenspring lodge sicken from the spring, not from Mee-Sei's food. Only Im-Moro, the spring-keeper, may go into the pool under the Hist. I'm to get into the pool, with her leave or without it at night.","directions":"The stone lip is on the lodge side of the pool; the Hist's roots go down into the water on the far side."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":2,"id":30,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.30","journal_text":"I have gone into the pool under the Hist at Greenspring. I'm to search the spring's throat between the roots, where the water comes up."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":3,"id":40,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.40","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.local.lh38|3:on_enter","journal_text":"A dead man lies staked in the throat of the spring at Greenspring, his wrists tied with rope, the stake left blank. That is what sickens the guests. I'm to find out who he was and who killed him, before the killer leaves.","directions":"The lodge store is the locked room behind Haj-Tei's door; Reeh-Shaal sleeps in the lodge and goes to the stone lip after the lamps are out."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":4,"id":50,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.50","journal_text":"The courier who vanished from the Greenspring lodge twelve days ago lies in the spring, and what I have found points to Reeh-Shaal, the guest who says she waits for a boat to Helstrom. I'm to confront her with what I hold, and I need two things to make it stand."}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":5,"id":70,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.70","ending":"complete","journal_text":"I named Reeh-Shaal before the people of Greenspring as the one who killed the Helstrom courier and staked him in the spring. Im-Moro has had the body raised and given to the Hist, and the root-herald holds Reeh-Shaal for Helstrom.","ending_id":"e-justice"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":6,"id":71,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.71","ending":"complete","journal_text":"Reeh-Shaal is dead by my hand at Greenspring. Im-Moro has had the courier's body raised from the spring, and the guests should mend.","ending_id":"e-fight"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":7,"id":72,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.72","ending":"complete","journal_text":"I took the sealed packet from Reeh-Shaal at Greenspring and let her go. Nobody there will learn who killed the courier.","ending_id":"e-deal"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":8,"id":80,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.80","ending":"failed","journal_text":"I accused Tsono-Ra of the courier's murder at Greenspring, and I was wrong. The village has closed ranks against me, and Reeh-Shaal has taken the boat.","ending_id":"e-wrong"}
{"quest_id":"quest.local.lh38","ord":9,"id":90,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.lh38.90","ending":"failed","journal_text":"Reeh-Shaal has left Greenspring on the Helstrom boat. Whoever killed the courier in the spring has gone, and the guests are still sick.","ending_id":"e-unsolved"}
