{"quest_id":"quest.main.mq32","ord":0,"id":10,"place":"place.hist-heartland.helstrom","outside_packet":"4.3"}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":0,"id":10,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.10","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.mr.mr01|0:on_enter","journal_text":"Root-Herald Ixo-Vaal of Greenspring asked me, for the Many-Root Conclave, to find out why the village's Hist is sickening. The village blames the salt works upstream. I'm to test the water before I believe them.","directions":"The fork lies a short walk upstream of the river landing; the herald's house, with the salt sack at its door, faces the Hist."}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":1,"id":20,"place":"place.hist-heartland.root-gallery-drowned-stair","journal":"text.journal.mr01.20","outside_packet":"4.2.hist-heartland","journal_text":"The salt in Greenspring's spring is not coming down the river. The couriers say the Hist's roots run into the flooded galleries of the Drowned Stair. I'm to go down and take water at each landing.","directions":"From Greenspring take the road to the Gate-Side Camp outside Helstrom's gate; the guides there show the stair's mouth, where the deep water starts."}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":2,"id":30,"place":"place.hist-heartland.root-gallery-drowned-stair","journal":"text.journal.mr01.30","outside_packet":"4.2.hist-heartland","journal_text":"The water in the Drowned Stair grows saltier the deeper I go. I'm to reach the deepest chamber, beyond one breath, and see where the salt comes in."}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":3,"id":40,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.40","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.mr.mr01|3:on_enter","journal_text":"Deep in the Drowned Stair, a channel has been cut by hand into a brine seam, and the floods push the brine into Greenspring's roots. The cut is old. I'm to learn who made it, and Vees-Wai, the tree-minder, reads the old stakes."}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":4,"id":50,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.50","on_enter":"quest_stage:quest.mr.mr01|4:on_enter","journal_text":"Greenspring's founders cut the channel to kill a rival grove downstream, and their deed is killing their own Hist. Ixo-Vaal has called the office-holders to the Hist. I'm to put what I found before them and argue for a cure, and for whether the founders are named."}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":5,"id":60,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.60","ending":"complete","journal_text":"The office-holders of Greenspring sealed the founders' cut and named the deed at the Hist. The tree should mend, and Greenspring now owes the people of the dead grove an answer.","ending_id":"e-sealed-named"}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":6,"id":61,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.61","ending":"complete","journal_text":"The office-holders of Greenspring sealed the founders' cut and agreed to say nothing of who made it. The tree should mend.","ending_id":"e-sealed-silent"}
{"quest_id":"quest.mr.mr01","ord":7,"id":62,"place":"place.hist-heartland.greenspring","journal":"text.journal.mr01.62","ending":"complete","journal_text":"Greenspring chose to reopen the founders' cut downstream. Their Hist is spared, and the dead grove's land will flood with brine again.","ending_id":"e-reopened"}
